{"key":"soilsurf","updated":"2026-10-24","label":"Surface soil moisture","title":"Surface soil moisture (0–5 cm) compared with normal","subtitle":"Sep 2026, against Sep in 11 earlier years","source":"NASA SMAP L4 (SPL4SMGP v008)","demo":false,"build":1,"categories":[{"key":"very_dry","label":"Very dry","color":"#8c510a","note":"driest 10% of years"},{"key":"dry","label":"Dry","color":"#d8b365","note":"driest 10 to 30% of years"},{"key":"normal","label":"Near normal","color":"#f3efe4","note":"middle 40% of years"},{"key":"wet","label":"Wet","color":"#5ab4ac","note":"wettest 10 to 30% of years"},{"key":"very_wet","label":"Very wet","color":"#01665e","note":"wettest 10% of years"},{"key":"not_rated","label":"Not rated","note":"no usable land cell","color":"#bdbdbd"}],"rank":{"high":"Wettest compared with normal","low":"Driest compared with normal","note":"Ranked by surface soil moisture as a percentage of normal."},"how":"The top 5 cm of soil is what a seed or seedling meets first. It dries out and wets up within days, so it can be far from the root zone. This shows the monthly average for that layer compared with the same month in every year since 2015.","limits":["The values come from NASA SMAP Level 4, which feeds satellite readings into a land model. They are modelled estimates and not measurements at depth.","The record starts in 2015, so normal rests on a few earlier years and the rankings are coarse.","The grid is about 9 km, so it works for parish averages and not for single fields. Coastal parishes include a lot of water and wetland.","The surface layer reacts to single rains and hot spells, so a monthly average can hide a wet week and a dry week."],"credits":[{"text":"Soil moisture: NASA SMAP L4 (SPL4SMGP), NSIDC DAAC","url":"https://nsidc.org/data/spl4smgp"},{"text":"Parish boundaries: US Census Bureau cartographic boundary files (public domain)","url":"https://www.census.gov/geographies/mapping-files/time-series/geo/cartographic-boundary.html"}],"chart":{"k